 "summary": "Commodities were broadly firmer in the latest session, with 17 of the 24 tracked benchmarks higher and 6 lower. Energy advanced across the board, led by Coal (Newcastle) at +2.19% to 144.85 USD/T; precious metals were mixed, 4 of 5 higher, the biggest move coming from Palladium at +2.14% to 1359 USD/t oz; base metals were mixed, 2 of 6 higher, the biggest move coming from Zinc at -1.32% to 3856.40 USD/T; bulk and battery materials were mixed, 3 of 5 higher, the biggest move coming from Iron Ore 62% Fe at +3.41% to 99.33 USD/T; agriculture advanced across the board, led by Sugar at +1.72% to 18.68 USd/Lbs. The largest single move across the complex was Iron Ore 62% Fe at +3.41%. Coal (Newcastle), Tin, Iron Ore 62% Fe, Uranium (U3O8) have not refreshed past the prior day's print and are flagged accordingly, being fixed periodically rather than traded continuously. Rare earths are represented by the MP Materials equity proxy, as no reliable daily spot benchmark is published. Reported alongside the session, Bitget on 01 September 2026:",
